==Finnish==

===Adjective===
{{fi-adj|tumm|empi|in}}

# [[dark]] [[colour]]
#:''Hänellä on tumma tukka. (She has dark hair.)''
#:''Naapurin jätkä seurustelee taas sen tumman tytön kanssa.'' The guy next door dates the dark-haired girl again.

====Usage notes====
As an adjective, ''tumma'' normally describes the subject to be dark of color. If a person is the subject, it often just means that they have dark hair and possibly dark eyes, and not necessarily that their skin color was dark. Also it doesn't necessarily mean that the person in question was a gypsy.

====Declension====
{{fi-decl-koira|tumm|||a|}}

====Antonyms====
*[[vaalea]]

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# (person) [[gypsy]], [[Rom]]
#:''Naapurin jätkän tyttökaveri vaikuttaa olevan tumma.''
#:*The next door guy's girlfriend appears to be a gypsy.
#:''Tummat kruisasivat Mersullaan kylän halki.''
#:*The gypsies cruised through the town in their Mercedes Benz.

====Usage notes====
As a reference to any number greater than one of gypsies, the word is used in the plural case ''tummat''. The singular case is seldom (although increasingly often) used alone in reference to one gypsy. 

====Declension====
{{fi-decl-koira|tumm}}

